Make ONLY the following compatibility change in my frontend/app.js.

1. Find this exact line:

ts.candleMarkers = LightweightCharts.createSeriesMarkers(ts.candles);

Replace it with:

ts.candleMarkers = null;


2. Find this exact block in runForecast():

if (data.signals && data.signals.length > 0) {
    ts.candleMarkers.setMarkers(toChartMarkers(data.signals));
} else {
    ts.candleMarkers.setMarkers([]);
}

Replace it with:

if (ts.candleMarkers) {
    if (data.signals && data.signals.length > 0) {
        ts.candleMarkers.setMarkers(toChartMarkers(data.signals));
    } else {
        ts.candleMarkers.setMarkers([]);
    }
}

Do NOT change anything else in app.js, app.py, TCN, GRU, predictor, forecast logic, SignalEngine, API payloads, chart configuration, or indicators.

The purpose of this change is only to prevent LightweightCharts.createSeriesMarkers() from stopping JavaScript initialization if the loaded Lightweight Charts version does not support that API.
